
  Worktrees
  Worktrees folder  ../.trees · default
                    Where new worktrees go, relative to the repository; outside it keeps the main
                    checkout clean
  Base branch       main · default
                    The branch new worktrees start from by default

  .env files
  .env from         copy
                    takes example, main, parent, none
                    ! env.strategy must be one of example, main, parent, none, not copy
                    Where a new worktree's .env files come from: a fresh checkout has none of your
                    local ones
  .env files        apps/api/.env, apps/web/.env
                    The .env files every new worktree gets

  Hooks
  On create         pnpm install
                    pnpm db:generate · in packages/db
                    Commands run in a worktree once it is created, such as installing its dependencies
  On clean          docker compose down · goes on if it fails
                    Commands run in a worktree before it is removed, such as stopping what it started

  Remembered answers
  Env strategy      parent

